            <ArticleTitle>Endovascular stent placement for isolated spontaneous dissection of the superior mesenteric artery: report of a case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>520-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous dissection of the superior mesenteric artery (SMA) is rare and has been reported only sporadically. The therapeutic options are either a surgical approach, which is the most frequently adopted, or simple observation. We present a patient with acute abdominal pain due to superior mesenteric artery dissection who was successfully treated by percutaneous endovascular stent placement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
